# --- Generated API types -----------------------------------------------------
# `src/api/generated/` is regenerated with `npm run api:types` (ADR-029) and is never
# hand-edited — but it **is** committed, and this is the note explaining why it is not
# listed here.
#
# It used to be ignored, and that broke the repository in two ways at once:
#
#  1. `src/api/types.ts` does `import type { components } from './generated/schema'`, so
#     a fresh clone could not typecheck or build at all. `tsc -b` failed with
#     `TS2307: Cannot find module './generated/schema'`, every type derived from
#     `components` collapsed to `any`, and `eslint` then reported **566**
#     `no-unsafe-*` errors across 14 files. That is what was failing CI, not the code.
#  2. The `contract` job's own check is `git diff --exit-code src/api/generated/` — which
#     can only ever mean anything if the file is tracked. Ignoring it made the one job
#     that exists to stop hand-editing generated code silently vacuous.
#
# Committing it keeps ADR-029 intact: the file is still generated, and the `contract` job
# regenerates it and fails on any difference, so a hand edit is still caught. What
# changes is that the build is now hermetic — a clone builds without first needing the
# backend repository next to it.

